+# AuraLite-Render — status
+
+Date: 2026-10-31. Host: OpenJDK 11, Linux x86_64, 2 CPUs.
+Every number below is measured by `make test`, not estimated.
+
+## Host gates: 7/7 green
+
+```
+rhi         51 passed   0 failed   0 NC   PASS
+graph       81 passed   0 failed   1 NC   PASS
+uniform     91 passed   0 failed   0 NC   PASS
+biome      142 passed   0 failed   1 NC   PASS
+nulldev    115 passed   0 failed   0 NC   PASS
+pack       147 passed   0 failed   0 NC   PASS
+tables     340 passed   0 failed   0 NC   PASS
+TOTAL 967 passed, 0 failed, 2 negative controls, 7/7 suites green
+RESULT: PASS
+```
+
+(Timings excluded: the receipt is the counts plus PASS, never microseconds.)
+
+## What the receipts prove
+
+- **rhi**: 42 formats, 13 stages, 27 capabilities behind one backend-agnostic interface.
+- **graph**: 8 passes declared, 7 ordered (`cloud_shadow, shadow_map, terrain, ssao,
+  lighting, taa_resolve, present`); 14 barriers planned, 0 suppressed; 1 alias group
+  reclaiming 2097152 B; 79116288 B owned textures. The disabled pass names its
+  option (`unused_debug -- option 'DEBUG_VIEW' is off`).
+- **uniform**: variadic OptiFine/Iris `if()` accepted as a 28-part chain; smooth
+  interpolation measured frame by frame (`frame1=0.064493 frame2=0.124827`).
+- **biome**: water colour across a swamp|plains border in ONE frame — 7 sample
+  positions, 5 distinct colours, 3 strictly intermediate; seam structurally one
+  4-block cell. Bake: one unmodified legacy expression → 2 spatially distinct
+  water colours in an 8×4×8 volume (4096 B). Iris can express 1.
+- **nulldev**: 14 commands recorded, 18 violations refused and named; leak gate:
+  40 handles created, 0 live after `close()`; idle-device receipts byte-identical.
+- **pack**: native pack parses with 0 errors — 7 passes, 7 programs, 12 files /
+  738 B, one vertex-only shadow warning. Native frame: 50 commands, 17 barriers,
+  8160 work groups, 0 violations. Legacy pack: 6 programs, 7 options, coverage
+  6/40; legacy frame 5 passes, 35 commands, 8 barriers, 0 violations.
+  `ceil(1080/16) = 68` — the dispatch covers every edge pixel.
+- **tables**: GL maps 39/42 formats (no sized sRGB R/RG storage in core GL),
+  VK 41 + `UNDEFINED`→0; every enum literal verified against the spec value
+  (`RGBA8=0x8058`, `BC1_SRGB=0x8C4C`, `RGBA8_SRGB=43`, `D32S8=130`,
+  `BC7_SRGB=146`); barrier stages derived from access masks and pinned
+  (`SHADER_READ → COMPUTE|FRAGMENT`, `MEMORY → ALL_COMMANDS`).
+  The tables load with no LWJGL on the classpath — inlined constants only.
+
+## Lanes
+
+| Lane | State |
+|---|---|
+| core: rhi, graph, scene, uniform, biome, pack | done, gated |
+| backend-null (recording + fail-fast) | done, gated |
+| core: util (`Checks`, `MathUtil`, `Extents`) | done, gated |
+| backend-gl (GL 4.6, LWJGL, compile-verified) | done, compiles rc=0 |
+| backend-vulkan (VK 1.3, LWJGL, compile-verified) | done, compiles rc=0 |
+| docs (README, ROADMAP, api/, plans/) | next |
+| tools (packlint, drift-check) | after docs |
+| packs/AuraLite-Native | after tools |
+| fabric/ (Java 21 + Gradle/Loom) | source + json only; build lane SKIPs (needs JDK 21) |
+| patches/ (one .patch per phase) | at phase close |
+
+## Backends (compile-verified, no GPU in this sandbox)
+
+- **GL** (`GlDevice` + `GlCommandBuffer`, ~1450 lines): immediate execution,
+  `submit` is a flush; semantic DSA; push constants via a reserved 128 B UBO;
+  descriptor unit = `set*16+binding`; RHI viewports flipped against pass height;
+  FBO cache with hex completeness codes; handle 0 = the window, never mixed
+  with offscreen targets; SPIR-V where `GL_ARB_gl_spirv` exists, GLSL otherwise.
+- **Vulkan** (`VkDevice` + `VkCommandBuffer`, ~2300 lines): instance → device,
+  validation behind `AURALITE_VK_VALIDATION=1`; discrete-GPU pick; per-family
+  command pools; per-image layout tracker that wins over the graph's from-state
+  (uploads happen outside the graph); render-pass keys include incoming layouts
+  so LOAD passes survive frame 2; grow-only descriptor pools; mesh/ray features
+  enabled when the driver offers them, capabilities reported accordingly.
+- Both refuse foreign resources by name, enforce usage flags exactly like NULL,
+  and keep the same failure vocabulary (`GfxException` with backend + offender).
+
+Standing rule: host-buildable code stays Java 11 source-compatible so `make test`
+is genuinely green here. `third_party/` holds gitignored LWJGL 3.4.3 jars fetched
+by `make deps` (~11 MB); they are compile-only and never committed.
diff --git a/docs/api/PACK_FORMAT.md b/docs/api/PACK_FORMAT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1c79216
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/api/PACK_FORMAT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,171 @@
+# Pack format, API level 1
+
+Authority for both modes. When this doc and a loader disagree, the loader is
+a bug — except the loader is also the gate, so check the suite first.
+
+`CURRENT_API_LEVEL = 1`. A pack declaring higher is refused with both numbers
+named. A pack declaring lower (or nothing) loads; the loader never guesses.
+
+## Detection
+
+Checked in order, first match wins:
+
+1. `pack.aurapack` exists → NATIVE.
+2. `shaders/shaders.properties` exists → LEGACY_IRIS.
+3. `shaders.properties` exists at root → LEGACY_IRIS.
+4. A non-empty `shaders/` tree exists → LEGACY_IRIS (markerless legacy).
+5. Neither → refused: "this does not look like a shader pack".
+
+Both trees present → NATIVE, and the report records that the legacy tree was
+ignored. Silence is not a detection strategy.
+
+Legacy dimensions, in scan order: `""`, `world-1/`, `world1/`, `world0/`.
+Program names come from filenames against 40 real on-disk names
+(`gbuffers_terrain`, `shadow`, `composite`, …); unknown names are warnings,
+not errors, and coverage is reported as `k of 40`.
+
+## NATIVE: `pack.aurapack`
+
+INI-shaped, `#` comments, `key = value`. Eight sections; anything before the
+first `[section]` is an error, an unknown section is a warning. Values are
+trimmed; keys are case-sensitive.
+
+### [meta]
+
+`name`, `version`, `author`, `description` — all plain strings.
+`auralite.api` (or bare `api`) — integer, must be ≤ 1. Absent means 1.
+
+### [capabilities]
+
+Two keys, comma-separated `GfxCapability` names:
+
+```
+require = COMPUTE_SHADERS, TEXTURE_3D, INTEGER_TEXTURES
+optional = RAY_QUERY
+```
+
+A missing `require` fails the load against a device with the capability
+named. `optional` is advisory: the pack is expected to branch on it.
+
+### [biome]
+
+```
+spatialUniforms = true
+sampleEntries = 4
+```
+
+`spatialUniforms` opts the pack into the baked 3D biome field (see the biome
+notes): legacy `if(in(biome,…))` expressions evaluate per cell at bake time
+instead of per fragment. Truthy: `true`, `1`, `yes`, `on`.
+
+### [resources]
+
+One line per image: `name = format tokens…`. The format is a `GfxFormat`
+name (`rgba8_unorm`, `rgba16f`, `d32_sfloat`, `r16f`, `rgba8_uint`, …);
+unknown formats are errors.
+
+Size tokens (one wins; default is fullscreen):
+
+| Token | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `fullscreen` | swapchain-sized, follows the window |
+| `shadow` | shadow-map sized, implies depth usage |
+| `scaled=f` / `scaled f` | fullscreen × factor (SSAO at `scaled=0.5`) |
+| `WxH` / `WxHxD` | fixed pixels, e.g. `256x256` |
+| `biome-volume` | the baked biome field; implies 3D + sampled |
+| `3d` | a 3D image with the current size kind |
+| `mips=N` / `layers=N` | mip count / array layers |
+
+Other tokens: `history` (keeps `.prev` alongside `.cur` for TAA-style
+passes), `imported` (the host binds it, e.g. the backbuffer),
+`usage=a|b|c` with flags `sampled storage color depth present transient
+input transfer-src transfer-dst`. Unknown usage flags warn, unknown tokens
+error.
+
+With no `usage=` token, depth formats default to `sampled|depth` and
+everything else to `sampled|color`. The default covers the common case;
+passes that need more say so.
+
+### [options]
+
+```
+CLOUD_QUALITY = select "Raymarch steps" { 14=Cheap, 24=Standard, 36=High } default=24 tab=Atmosphere
+SSAO = bool "Screen-space ambient occlusion" default=true tab=Lighting
+BLOOM_STRENGTH = slider 0.0..2.0 step 0.05 "Bloom" default=0.35 tab=Colour
+```
+
+Grammar: `NAME = kind "label" [{ v=Label, … }] [default=v] [tab=T]`.
+Kinds: `bool`, `const`, `slider`, `select`/`selector`, `define` (the default
+when no kind is given). `bool` gains `true/false` choices automatically.
+Sliders carry their range in the head: `slider min..max step s`.
+Unterminated labels and choice blocks are errors; unknown kinds are errors.
+
+Options become `#define` lines (`#define CLOUD_QUALITY 36`, `#define SSAO`,
+`#define BLOOM_STRENGTH 0.35`) and gate passes through `when=`.
+
+### [graph]
+
+Passes first, then the present pointer:
+
+```
+pass cloud_shadow raster color=cloud_shadow program=cloud_shadow
+pass ssao compute write=ao read=scene_depth program=ssao dispatch=ceil(width/16),ceil(height/16),1 when=SSAO
+pass present raster color=backbuffer read=taa.cur external program=final
+present = taa
+```
+
+`pass <name> <raster|compute|copy> [clauses…]`. A pass line carries `=` inside
+its own clause list, so it is split on whitespace, not on `=` — that special
+case is load-bearing, not incidental.
+
+Clauses: `color`/`colors`, `depth`, `read`/`reads`, `write`/`writes`,
+`program`, `when` (option name; a pass whose option is off is culled and
+names the option), `dispatch` (three comma-separated extent expressions for
+compute), bare `external` (touches the imported backbuffer). History resources
+address sides explicitly: `taa.cur`, `taa.prev`.
+
+The graph builder orders passes by semantic RAW/WAW edges plus a declaration
+tie-break — never by declaration order alone — plans barriers, and culls
+passes no kept pass reads. Load-bearing passes survive via `keep(why)`.
+
+`present = <resource>` names what reaches the screen.
+
+### [programs]
+
+```
+ssao = shaders/ssao.comp local_size=16x16x1
+terrain = shaders/terrain.vert, shaders/terrain.frag
+shadow = shaders/shadow.vert pass=shadow_map
+```
+
+`name = path[, path…] [attr=…]…`. Attributes: `local_size` (also
+`localSize`, `WxHxD`), `pass` (binds the program to a pass by name).
+Stages come from extensions (`.vert .frag .comp`, …).
+
+NATIVE never infers filenames: every stage is listed. A raster program
+without a vertex stage is a load error; a missing fragment stage is a
+warning, because depth-only shadow passes are legal and common.
+
+### [screen]
+
+Tabs, one per line: `Atmosphere = CLOUD_QUALITY`. The left side is the tab
+name, the right lists that tab's options; matching names are tabbed onto
+their options, the rest are kept verbatim for the UI lane to resolve.
+A tab pointing nowhere is a pack bug, but the loader reports it — it does
+not refuse the pack over a menu.
+
+## LEGACY_IRIS: `shaders.properties`
+
+Read as shipped: block/item/entity IDs, custom uniforms with OptiFine/Iris
+expression syntax (`if`, `in`, `smooth`, `mix`, variadic chains), filename
+→ program mapping per dimension. The expression evaluator is shared with the
+uniform lane and gated there (28-part `if` chains, float `/`, frame-by-frame
+`smooth`). Spatial biome uniforms stay off unless the host opts in with
+`auralite.spatialBiomeUniforms=true`, which injects `AURALITE_SPATIAL_BIOME`
+(default false) and freezes `smooth()` state at bake time.
+
+## The load report
+
+Every load returns errors, warnings, and notes together. Errors refuse the
+pack; warnings load it loudly; notes record decisions (NATIVE-over-both,
+inferred filenames, culled passes). `packlint` is this report as a CLI.
diff --git a/docs/api/RHI.md b/docs/api/RHI.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ffcb064
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/api/RHI.md
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# RHI: the device contract
+
+`dev.auralite.render.rhi`. One interface, three implementations (NULL, GL,
+Vulkan). If two backends disagree, NULL — the recording reference — settles it.
+
+## Resources
+
+Created from descriptors, destroyed explicitly, never garbage-collected
+quietly: the leak gate counts 40 handles created, 0 live after `close()`.
+
+- **Buffers**: size, usage flags (`VERTEX INDEX UNIFORM STORAGE INDIRECT
+  TRANSFER_SRC/DST`), memory domain. Host-visible buffers map; device-local
+  buffers upload through staging.
+- **Images**: format (42 in `GfxFormat`), size kind, mips, layers, samples,
+  usage. Compressed images are single-level by construction: GL clamps the
+  level count to 1 and uploads them with the compressed entry points, Vulkan
+  refuses `mips>1`/multisampled at creation and staged uploads entirely
+  (block math is a named v2 gap, not a silent clamp).
+- **Samplers, shader modules, pipelines**: descriptors in, validated handles
+  out. SPIR-V is the interchange; GLSL source is accepted on GL and refused
+  on Vulkan with the offline-compile message.
+- **Descriptors**: sets are written against a pipeline layout and validated
+  at bind — kind, resource type, usage flag, array bounds. A write that does
+  not match the layout names the set, the binding, and both sides.
+
+Foreign resources are refused by name at every entry point: a GL buffer
+handed to the Vulkan device fails with the call and the offender, never
+with a native crash.
+
+## Commands
+
+Command buffers are one-shot: `begin()`, record, `end()`, submit once.
+Recording outside `begin()/end()` is refused; `end()` with a pass open is
+refused without killing the buffer.
+
+- **Raster**: `beginRenderPass` (area checked against every attachment at
+  its mip), viewport/scissor (RHI origin is top-left on all backends),
+  pipeline + vertex/index bindings, direct/indirect/indexed draws.
+- **Compute**: pipeline, `dispatch` ( extents checked against device limits),
+  `dispatchIndirect`. Dispatch inside a render pass is refused.
+- **Transfers**: buffer↔buffer, buffer→image, image→image, blits (linear on
+  depth or integer images is refused), mipmap generation.
+- **Barriers**: image (state + access pair), buffer (access pair),
+  `memoryBarrierAll`. Push constants and timestamps round out the set.
+
+Every command validates usage flags exactly like NULL does. Indirect
+strides default honestly: 16 bytes for arrays, 20 for indexed.
+
+## Backends
+
+| | GL 4.6 | Vulkan 1.3 |
+|---|---|---|
+| Execution | immediate; `submit` is a flush | recorded, one-shot submit |
+| Descriptors | unit = `set*16+binding` | grow-only pools, allocated per bind |
+| Push constants | reserved 128 B UBO | one range, stages from the layout |
+| Layouts | none (API has none) | tracked per image; the tracker wins over stale graph state |
+| Render passes | FBO cache, hex completeness | cached, keyed with incoming layouts so LOAD survives frame 2 |
+| Timestamps | 64-query ring, capture-oriented | 256-query pool, reset per frame |
+| Shaders | SPIR-V via `GL_ARB_gl_spirv`, else GLSL | SPIR-V only |
+
+Neither backend owns a swapchain: presentation is fabric glue. Handle 0 on
+GL is the window's default framebuffer and is never mixed with offscreen
+targets. Validation layers (Vulkan) and the debug callback (GL) are wired
+but quiet unless the host asks.
+
+## Capabilities and limits
+
+`GfxCapability` (27) is the pack-facing vocabulary: what the pack may
+require. `GfxLimits` is the numeric side: work-group counts, viewport and
+texture bounds, descriptor and push-constant ceilings. Backends report only
+capabilities the RHI can actually exercise — a flag the API cannot back is
+a lie, and lies fail the gate.
